  "step_3": "The decision reason requires adjusting probabilities for outcomes with probabilities below 20%, but in this case, all probabilities (33%, 34%, 66%, 67%) are above 20%, so the reason does not apply. The individual’s deliberation focuses on expected value (probability × outcome) and the relative size of payoff vs. probability differences, which is consistent with expected utility reasoning, not the specified reason. Since the decision reason is inapplicable to the problem (no low-probability outcomes to adjust), and the individual did not mention any adjustment of probabilities or consideration of low-probability outcomes, there is no evidence that the individual used this reason. The individual’s justification does not align with the rule of the reason, nor was the reason applicable. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
